From: hjviewer <build@hjviewer.invalid>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 20:24:41 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 064/160] hjviewer: serialize quiet device-list refreshes

Keep request-in-flight state separate from the visible loading indicator.
Foreground and wake completion refresh the device list quietly, so using
only groupLoading as the guard allowed overlapping HTTP requests for the
same URLs. Release the guard and complete cache waiters in finally,
before notifying loading observers that might throw.

Allow cache reads during a quiet refresh, but defer applying them until
the request completes. Invalidate pending reads when a new list is
applied, reset, or cleared by access policy. Preserve offline cache
recovery on failed requests, whether the read starts or finishes before
or during the request. Keep visible-refresh cache skipping unchanged.

Save cache only when the list revision changes, so a failed refresh
cannot overwrite the on-disk offline cache with an uninitialized list.
Keep 401 handling ahead of saving and retain initialized semantics.

Source-body Dart regression scenarios exercise requests, cache races,
and cache writes. This does not replace Flutter/FFI integration validation.
